# TradeSense Institutional System — Cursor AI Operating Rules (.cursorrules)
# Applies to: Cursor, Windsurf, GitHub Copilot, and Cline

# 1. Environment & Execution
- Virtual Environment: C:\Python Virtual Environments\Personal Projects\TradeSense\Scripts\python.exe
- Test Suite: Always verify with `python -m pytest tests/ -v`
- App Launch: `streamlit run src/ui/app.py`

# 2. Financial & Microstructure Domain Invariants
- Zero Lookahead Bias: Always construct forward targets via df["Close"].shift(-1). Never calculate predictive features on contemporaneous or future bars.
- Mathematical Monotonicity: Quantile predictions must guarantee P10 <= P50 <= P90 at 100% rate using softplus positive offsets.
- Fractional Multi-Asset Sizing: High-priced assets (BTC, ETH) must use fractional float sizing (round to 4 decimals for price >= 1000). Never truncate order quantity to int(0).
- Candlestick Chart Category Collision: When using Plotly category x-axis, all label strings must be uniquely formatted (_format_chart_time_labels) so bars never collapse into stacked monoliths.
- Continuous Candle Aggregation: Ticks update active candle; completed bars hand off Open = previous Close.
- Intra-bar Polarity: Bullish bars evaluate Stop-Loss at Low before Take-Profit at High. Bearish bars evaluate Take-Profit at High before Stop-Loss at Low.
- Dynamic Trailing Stops: Trailing stop floors can only ratchet upwards for long positions; they must never decrease.

# 3. Strategy & Signal Protocol
- In any BaseStrategy implementation or ensemble, always resolve reference price: price = float(df["Close"].iloc[current_idx]) before computing percentage-based target/stop levels to avoid NameError.
- Never block the UI with full-page st.rerun() loops. Always use @st.fragment(run_every="2s").
